export const html = "<p class=\"lead\">Warehouse safety talks revolve around racks, forklifts and floors. But what about the pallets — the actual interface between your product and your racking?</p>\n    <p>Improper pallet use is one of the most underestimated causes of rack damage. Cracked pallets, over- or undersized loads and mismatched designs quietly change how weight reaches the beam — and where the weight lands matters as much as how much of it there is.</p>\n\n    <h2 id=\"wrong\">The pallet problem: what can go wrong</h2>\n    <ul class=\"clean risk\">\n      <li><strong>Damaged pallets</strong> — splintered decks or broken runners give uneven, unreliable bearing on the beam, and can fail outright under load.</li>\n      <li><strong>Inconsistent sizes</strong> — non-standard pallets don’t align with the beam supports, so the load isn’t carried where the beam expects it.</li>\n      <li><strong>Improper stacking</strong> — overhanging or misaligned pallets stress the beams and rack corners, and put weight outside the support.</li>\n      <li><strong>Wrong pallet type</strong> — non-rackable or reversible pallets on selective racking can deflect or fail.</li>\n      <li><strong>Concentrated loads</strong> — a single heavy pallet placed mid-span, or weight bunched in the middle of a pallet, overstresses the beam far more than the same weight spread out.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h2 id=\"bend\">Where the weight sits — a worked comparison</h2>\n    <p>A rack beam is rated for its load <strong>spread across it</strong>. Move that load — or even a little less of it — into the middle, and the bending moment, stress and deflection all climb. Take the same beam under two loadings that weigh almost the same:</p>\n\n    <figure>\n      <svg class=\"art\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Left: three 750 kg pallets spread across a beam, which stays almost straight. Right: a single 2000 kg load at mid-span, which bends the beam noticeably more despite being lighter.\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n        <defs>\n          <marker id=\"ag2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><polygon points=\"0,0 9,0 4,8\" fill=\"#1F8A4C\"/></marker>\n          <marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"11\" markerHeight=\"11\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><polygon points=\"0,0 10,0 5,9\" fill=\"#C0392B\"/></marker>\n        </defs>\n        <rect width=\"900\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n        <line x1=\"450\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"450\" y2=\"300\" stroke=\"#E2E6EC\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n        <!-- LEFT spread -->\n        <text x=\"225\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Fraunces,serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#14365C\">3 × 750 kg — spread (2250 kg)</text>\n        <g stroke=\"#14365C\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"252\"/><line x1=\"380\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"252\"/></g>\n        <rect x=\"60\" y=\"188\" width=\"330\" height=\"9\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#14365C\"/>\n        <g fill=\"#DCE4EC\" stroke=\"#14365C\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"92\" y=\"152\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"186\" y=\"152\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"280\" y=\"152\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\"/></g>\n        <g fill=\"#1F8A4C\"><rect x=\"92\" y=\"152\" width=\"78\" height=\"4\"/><rect x=\"186\" y=\"152\" width=\"78\" height=\"4\"/><rect x=\"280\" y=\"152\" width=\"78\" height=\"4\"/></g>\n        <g stroke=\"#1F8A4C\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" marker-end=\"url(#ag2)\"><line x1=\"131\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"131\" y2=\"150\"/><line x1=\"225\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"225\" y2=\"150\"/><line x1=\"319\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"319\" y2=\"150\"/></g>\n        <text x=\"225\" y=\"286\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#176B3B\" font-weight=\"600\">beam stays straight — low moment</text>\n        <!-- RIGHT centred -->\n        <text x=\"675\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Fraunces,serif\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#14365C\">2000 kg — at the centre</text>\n        <g stroke=\"#14365C\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><line x1=\"520\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"520\" y2=\"252\"/><line x1=\"830\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"830\" y2=\"252\"/></g>\n        <path d=\"M520 192 Q675 232 830 192\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#C0392B\" stroke-width=\"9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n        <path d=\"M520 188 Q675 188 830 188\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9BA8B6\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n        <rect x=\"632\" y=\"150\" width=\"86\" height=\"26\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#C9D2DC\" stroke=\"#14365C\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"632\" y=\"150\" width=\"86\" height=\"5\" fill=\"#C0392B\"/>\n        <line x1=\"675\" y1=\"122\" x2=\"675\" y2=\"146\" stroke=\"#C0392B\" stroke-width=\"8\" marker-end=\"url(#ar2)\"/>\n        <text x=\"675\" y=\"286\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#C0392B\" font-weight=\"600\">beam bows — high moment</text>\n      </svg>\n      <figcaption>The three spread pallets act like a distributed load; the single centred pallet acts like a point load at mid-span.</figcaption>\n    </figure>\n\n    <table class=\"tbl\">\n      <tr><th>On the same beam · span 3.0 m</th><th>3 × 750 kg spread</th><th>2000 kg at the centre</th><th>Difference</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>Total load carried</td><td>2250 kg</td><td>2000 kg</td><td class=\"r\">≈ 11% <em>less</em></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Peak bending moment</td><td class=\"m\">843.75 kg·m&nbsp;&nbsp;(W·L ⁄ 8)</td><td>1500 kg·m&nbsp;&nbsp;(P·L ⁄ 4)</td><td class=\"up\">≈ 78% higher</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Peak bending stress</td><td class=\"m\">lower</td><td>higher</td><td class=\"up\">≈ 78% higher</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Peak deflection</td><td class=\"m\">lower</td><td>higher</td><td class=\"up\">≈ 42% more</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"callout\"><span class=\"lbl\">The maths</span>For a simply supported beam of span <strong>L = 3.0 m</strong> — the three spread pallets acting as a distributed load, the single pallet as a point load at mid-span:<br>\n    · Spread: M = W·L ⁄ 8 = 2250 × 3.0 ⁄ 8 = <strong>843.75 kg·m</strong> (≈ 8.28 kN·m)<br>\n    · Centred: M = P·L ⁄ 4 = 2000 × 3.0 ⁄ 4 = <strong>1500 kg·m</strong> (≈ 14.72 kN·m)<br>\n    So 1500 ⁄ 843.75 = <strong>1.78</strong> — the lighter centred load produces about <strong>78% more bending moment</strong> (and the same on stress, which follows the moment). The percentage holds for any span, since L cancels in the ratio; the 3.0 m span just gives the actual figures. <strong>Less weight, in the wrong place, does more damage.</strong></div>\n\n    <h2 id=\"elements\">How pallets affect each rack element</h2>\n    <h3>Beams</h3>\n    <p>Designed for a uniform distributed load. A concentrated or badly placed load raises the bending moment the beam has to resist — and it was never sized for that.</p>\n    <h3>Uprights</h3>\n    <p>Pick up amplified stress when pallets make the beams deflect unevenly, loading one side of the frame more than the other.</p>\n    <h3>Bracing</h3>\n    <p>Can be struck or displaced by a sagging or overhanging pallet.</p>\n    <h3>Baseplates</h3>\n    <p>Take repeated shock as forklifts nudge and re-position a badly fitting pallet again and again.</p>\n    <p class=\"pquote\">Cracked or bowed beams are often traced back to pallet abuse — not a design failure.</p>\n\n    <h2 id=\"standards\">What the standards say</h2>\n    <ul class=\"clean\">\n      <li><strong>EN 15635</strong> (safe use) stresses rackable pallets and even load distribution as part of using racking safely.</li>\n      <li><strong>EN 15512</strong> (design) is where the beam <strong>deflection limits</strong> come from — the basis the beam is rated against.</li>\n      <li><strong>ISO 6780</strong> specifies the modular pallet dimensions that align with global racking standards.</li>\n      <li><strong>OEMs</strong> specify the allowable pallet types and orientations for each racking model.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>Ignore these and you expose the rack to damage that’s hard to spot but cumulative — it builds up quietly, load after load.</p>\n\n    <h2 id=\"myths\">Common misunderstandings</h2>\n    <table class=\"tbl\">\n      <tr><th>The myth</th><th>The reality</th></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"m\">Any pallet fits any rack</td><td class=\"r\">Only rack-compatible pallets should be used — shape, runner style and material all matter.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"m\">Wooden pallets absorb the damage</td><td class=\"r\">They often pass the stress straight into the rack without showing damage themselves.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"m\">If the total load is within rating, it’s fine</td><td class=\"r\">The wrong load pattern can overstress a beam locally, even under its rated weight.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"m\">A beam failure means a design flaw</td><td class=\"r\">It’s often the result of poor loading, not the design.</td></tr>\n    </table>\n\n    <h2 id=\"do\">What you can do</h2>\n    <ul class=\"clean do\">\n      <li>Audit all pallets in use — sort by condition, size and type.</li>\n      <li>Match the pallet design to the rack configuration (selective vs drive-in vs push-back).</li>\n      <li>Train forklift operators to place pallets fully and evenly on both beams.</li>\n      <li>Replace broken pallets immediately.</li>\n      <li>Avoid single heavy loads stranded mid-span; spread the load across the beam where you can.</li>\n      <li>Watch the beam deflection zones for the tell-tale signs of stress.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <p>In most warehouses, the racks aren’t failing — the pallets, and the way they’re loaded, are, and they’re passing that failure into the racks. Safe pallet use isn’t just logistics hygiene; it’s structural-integrity protection. RAMS lets you track not only rack health but the pallet patterns that cause long-term damage — because smart racks start with smart loading.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"cta\">\n      <h3>Find the high-risk pallet patterns first</h3>\n      <p>Build a digital twin of your storage zone and surface the pallet-rack interface problems before they cost you.</p>\n      <a class=\"btn\" href=\"/company/contact\">Audit your pallet-rack interface</a>\n    </div>";
